From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hlink: data object, shortcuts, browse context stack (3548)

hlink: hyperlink data object, CreateFromData, shortcut files, browse context stack, URL translation

IHlink's IDataObject renders the "Hyperlink" clipboard format (the hyperlink saved with OleSaveToStream) as
HGLOBAL or stream, with QueryGetData, GetDataHere, EnumFormatEtc, GetCanonicalFormatEtc. HlinkCreateFromData and
HlinkQueryCreateFromData read that format or URL/Unicode/ANSI text. HlinkTranslateURL applies the URL scheme and
file guessing. HlinkSetSpecialReference writes the start/search page. Internet shortcut (.url) files:
HlinkCreateShortcut / FromString / FromMoniker, HlinkResolveShortcut / ToString / ToMoniker. OleSaveToStreamEx.
IHlinkBrowseContext: OnNavigateHlink keeps a real back/forward stack (entries get ids; HLID_PREVIOUS/NEXT/
STACKTOP/STACKBOTTOM now follow the stack order), QueryHlink, EnumNavigationStack (IEnumHLITEM), Clone, Close
(revokes registered objects). IHlink::GetStringReference with an absolute reference fails with E_FAIL for a
relative moniker without a site, and IHlink::Navigate reduces the moniker before binding (both recorded
as todo_wine in the conformance tests; the marks are removed).
